  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Use any avatar\n\n3. Use 3p tracking (headset and controllers)\n\nAs it was before you had to move like 10~20 cms in any direction for your whole avatar to move, and if you made small movements, you legs were stuck to the ground to some point, to make it look adequate, but now any small movement causes what's in the attached gif. And it also seems that overall avatar display FPS dropped to like 20~ while everything else is normal (can see my arms and body moving in frames [game runs at ~60]).\n\nAdding waist tracker doesn't anyhow affect the issue.\n\nIt's not limited to specific avatar, map or smth.\n\nTested on different avatars, maps etc.\n\nP.S. tried switching vrchat version to beta and back, both same issue.",
